idth ~1080? I'll set `.sv-404__featured` max-width 1032?) Fine \\u2014 I'll constrain `.sv-404__featured ul.products { max-width: 1032px; margin: 0 auto; }`. But careful about \\\"global selector YASAK\\\" \\u2014 `.sv-404__featured ul.products` is scoped. Good.\\n\\nHmm, wait. Actually, let me think again about the width: `.sv-404` main container will be centered text, narrow (720px). The featured section maybe wider (full content width, e.g., 1080px). I can make `.sv-404` a full-width wrapper (padding 72px 24px) and inner blocks: `.sv-404__inner { max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto; text-align: center; }` and `.sv-404__featured { max-width: 1080px; margin: 64px auto 0; }`.\\n\\nDesign decision for featured head: a small serif heading \\\"\\u00d6ne \\u00c7\\u0131kanlar\\\"? Or \\\"Koleksiyondan se\\u00e7meler\\\"? Keep Turkish, no jargon: \\\"\\u00d6ne \\u00c7\\u0131kanlar\\\" is fine. With a link to shop \\\"T\\u00fcm Koleksiyon\\\"? That duplicates \\\"Ma\\u011fazaya git\\\" but is a link-style, acceptable. I'll add heading + subtle it. Actually keep it simple: heading centered with silk underline pattern? The section title pattern is left-aligned with `.sv-section-title::after`. For the 404 featured, I'll do a simpler centered serif h2 at 22-26px, letter-spacing, then the grid.\\n\\nHmm, actually \\u2014 maybe simpler and cleaner: skip the featured-products heading entirely and just show 3 cards under a hairline separator with a small uppercase label \\\"\\u00d6NE \\u00c7IKANLAR\\\". Let me design:\\n\\n```\\n[hairline]\\n\\u00d6NE \\u00c7IKANLAR        (uppercase small, letter-spacing .22em, whisper/silk)\\n[card grid]\\n```\\n\\nFine.\\n\\nNow, SEO/a11y: h1 = \\\"Arad\\u0131\\u011f\\u0131n\\u0131z sayfay\\u0131 bulamad\\u0131k\\\". The 404 also has the \\\"404\\\" code element as small text (aria-hidden or not?). I'll include `<p class=\\\"sv-404__code\\\">404</p>` \\u2014 it's informative; keep accessible but aria-hidden to avoid redundancy? It's fine either way; I'll keep it not hidden but it's decorative... Actually screen readers reading \\\"404\\\" then the title is fine. Keep it simple, no aria-hidden. Hmm, the design: a small silk \\\"404\\\" overline is nice and consistent with the design language (uppercase tracking). I'll keep it.\\n\\nSearch form: WP search form. `action=home_url('/')`, input name=\\\"s\\\". Button label \\\"Ara\\\". Also use `<label for=\\\"sv-404-search\\\" class=\\\"sv-404__label\\\">Sitede ara</label>` visually-hidden.\\n\\nPlaceholder: \\\"\\u00dcr\\u00fcn veya sayfa ara\\u2026\\\" \\u2014 hmm, jargon-free Turkish. Good.\\n\\nButtons: \\\"Ana sayfaya d\\u00f6n\\\" (primary), \\\"Ma\\u011fazaya git\\\" (ghost). \\n\\nWait \\u2014 heading: \\\"Arad\\u0131\\u011f\\u0131n\\u0131z sayfay\\u0131 bulamad\\u0131k\\\". Buttons: \\\"Ana sayfaya d\\u00f6n\\\", \\\"Ma\\u011fazaya git\\\". Description: \\\"Ba\\u011flant\\u0131 ta\\u015f\\u0131nm\\u0131\\u015f veya adres yanl\\u0131\\u015f yaz\\u0131lm\\u0131\\u015f olabilir.\\\" Good.\\n\\nAlso `<title>` \\u2014 WP handles 404 title via core (\\\"Sayfa bulunamad\\u0131 \\u2013 Sutre\\\"). Fine.\\n\\nOne more consideration \\u2014 should the 404 template include the search results loop? No.\\n\\nEscaping: use esc_url, esc_attr, esc_html_e for theme text with 'sutre' domain.\\n\\nNow the CSS. Let me define blocks with the P83 marker consistent with theme style (`/* \\u2550\\u2550\\u2550 P83 \\u2014 404 SAYFASI \\u2550\\u2550\\u2550 */ ... /* \\u2550\\u2550\\u2550 /P83 \\u2550\\u2550\\u2550 */`). Append at END of style.css (after P77 block). Also include media queries \\u2264781 and \\u2264480 for mobile.\\n\\nCSS plan:\\n\\n```css\\n/* \\u2550\\u2550\\u2550 P83 \\u2014 404 SAYFASI (bo\\u015f i\\u00e7erik alan\\u0131 doldurma; scoped .sv-404*) \\u2550\\u2550\\u2550 */\\n.sv-404 {\\n\\tpadding: 72px 24px 88px;\\n}\\n.sv-404__inner {\\n\\tmax-width: 640px;\\n\\tmargin: 0 auto;\\n\\ttext-align: center;\\n}\\n.sv-404__code {\\n\\tfont-family: var(--font-sans);