entytwentyfive wp-child-theme-sutre-child` \\u2014 child theme of TT5 with classic PHP.\\n\\nNow, let me also double-check: does 404 page include the WooCommerce \\\"products\\\" CSS in the body? We don't care.\\n\\nOne more thing: since `.woocommerce` div wrapper would be created by the shortcode, and `#sutre-content .woocommerce` padding rule applies \\u2014 I'll add scoped reset.\\n\\nAlternatively, avoid the wrapper entirely by hand-building the loop (wp wrapper: my own `<div class=\\\"sv-404__products\\\">` + `woocommerce_product_loop_start()` \\u2192 ul.products directly inside my section). That avoids the `.woocommerce` wrapper padding issue entirely, and I control markup. But then I need the WP_Query + wp_reset_postdata (as the pack demands when adding queries).\\n\\nWhich is simpler/more robust? Hand-built loop:\\n\\n```php\\n<?php if ( function_exists( 'wc_get_products' ) ) :\\n\\t$sv404_ids = wc_get_products( array(\\n\\t\\t'status'     => 'publish',\\n\\t\\t'limit'      => 3,\\n\\t\\t'visibility' => 'catalog',\\n\\t\\t'featured'   => true,\\n\\t\\t'return'     => 'ids',\\n\\t\\t'orderby'    => 'date',\\n\\t\\t'order'      => 'DESC',\\n\\t) );\\n\\tif ( empty( $sv404_ids ) ) {\\n\\t\\t$sv404_ids = wc_get_products( array(\\n\\t\\t\\t'status'     => 'publish',\\n\\t\\t\\t'limit'      => 3,\\n\\t\\t\\t'visibility' => 'catalog',\\n\\t\\t\\t'return'     => 'ids',\\n\\t\\t\\t'orderby'    => 'date',\\n\\t\\t\\t'order'      => 'DESC',\\n\\t\\t) );\\n\\t}\\n\\tif ( ! empty( $sv404_ids ) ) :\\n\\t\\t$sv404_query = new WP_Query( array(\\n\\t\\t\\t'post_type'           => 'product',\\n\\t\\t\\t'post_status'         => 'publish',\\n\\t\\t\\t'post__in'            => $sv404_ids,\\n\\t\\t\\t'orderby'             => 'post__in',\\n\\t\\t\\t'posts_per_page'      => 3,\\n\\t\\t\\t'no_found_rows'       => true,\\n\\t\\t\\t'ignore_sticky_posts' => true,\\n\\t\\t) );\\n\\t\\tif ( $sv404_query->have_posts() ) :\\n?>\\n\\t<section class=\\\"sv-404__featured\\\" aria-labelledby=\\