d? unknown) so it will show 2 cards. I'll include it. It's \\\"mevcut WooCommerce sorgular\\u0131yla\\\" (wc_get_products + WP_Query) with wp_reset_postdata.\\n\\nHmm, but one risk: `wc_get_products` with `'featured' => true` requires WC 3.2+; fine (WC 11.1.0).\\n\\nAlso, `wc_get_products` with visibility 'catalog' \\u2192 includes out-of-stock depending on settings; fine.\\n\\nWait, actually, let me reconsider using `[products]` shortcode vs hand-loop once more. With `do_shortcode('[products limit=\\\"3\\\" columns=\\\"2\\\" paginate=\\\"false\\\"]')`:\\n- Pros: proven on home; handles everything internally (visibility, loop props, resets).\\n- Cons: adds `.woocommerce` wrapper div \\u2192 theme's `#sutre-content .woocommerce` padding rule hits it \\u2192 need scoped reset `.sv-404__featured .woocommerce { padding: 0; max-width: none; }`. Also it doesn't do \\\"featured\\\" unless best_selling etc. Could use `[products limit=\\\"3\\\" columns=\\\"2\\\" paginate=\\\"false\\\" on_sale=\\\"false\\\"]`... default recent.\\n\\nHmm, the `.woocommerce` wrapper also affects card CSS interplay: `ul.products li.product .button` etc. remain fine.\\n\\nActually you know what, there's one more decisive factor: the shop grid max-width rule `#sutre-content .woocommerce ul.products { max-width: 1032px; margin: 0 auto; }` applies to shortcode output (has .woocommerce ancestor) \\u2192 grid capped at 1032 and centered. With hand-loop I must cap myself. Both fine.\\n\\nI'll go with the hand-built loop for full markup control (no wrapper surprise), since the pack explicitly mentions \\\"sorgu ekliyorsan wp_reset_postdata() \\u015fart\\\" \\u2014 indicating they anticipate a manual query. I'll do it carefully.\\n\\nHmm, one thing to check: does `wc_get_template_part('content','product')` + `woocommerce_product_loop_start()` work outside shop context on the 404 page? Yes \\u2014 this is the standard pattern used by Woo shortcodes/related products. Related products does exactly: `woocomm