'll do that. Hmm, but must reset after: `wc_reset_loop()`? The loop props would leak to subsequent queries on the same page (page ends after; footer). To be clean: call `wc_set_loop_prop('columns', 2)` then after loop `wc_reset_loop()`. Hmm, `wc_reset_loop()` resets ALL loop props including name/columns to defaults for later loops (footer has no loops). Fine, I'll include it in the same cleanup step as wp_reset_postdata.\\n\\nActually \\u2014 simpler: skip wc_set_loop_prop entirely; `columns-4` class is cosmetic and CSS-driven. Extra API calls = more risk. Hmm, but a stray loop prop default... no leaks either way. I'll skip setting props (don't add what isn't needed), just wp_reset_postdata.\\n\\nNow the CSS. Also: hmm, wait \\u2014 one important thing: with the hand loop, `ul.products` appears inside `.sv-404__featured` \\u2014 the theme rule at 1207 (`@media (max-width:781px) { .sv-products { padding: 48px 20px; } ul.products { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 20px; } }`) applies globally \\u2192 mobile 1 col. Good.\\n\\nAlso `#sutre-content ul.products li.product h2...` etc. \\u2014 global.\\n\\nAlright. Now let me also decide about `sv-404__featured` margin-top and separator. And decide padding numbers.\\n\\nLet me now write the 404.php file.\\n\\nMarkup:\\n\\n```php\\n<?php\\n/**\\n * 404 \\u2014 \\\"sayfa bulunamad\\u0131\\\" \\u015fablonu (P83).\\n * K\\u00f6k neden: tema'da 404.php yoktu \\u2192 index.php have_posts() false iken hi\\u00e7bir \\u015fey\\n * basm\\u0131yordu ve #sutre-content tamamen bo\\u015f kal\\u0131yordu (pack-81 kan\\u0131t\\u0131).\\n * Klasik mimari: get_header()/get_footer() + tek CSS (style.css, .sv-404* bloklar\\u0131).\\n */\\nif ( ! defined( 'ABSPATH' ) ) { exit; }\\n\\nget_header();\\n?>\\n\\n<main class=\\\"sv-404\\\">\\n\\t<div class=\\\"sv-404__inner\\\">\\n\\t\\t<p class=\\\"sv-404__code\\\">404</p>\\n\\t\\t<h1 class=\\\"sv-404__title\\\"><?php esc_html_e( 'Arad\\u0131\\u011f\\u0131n\\u0131z sayfay\\u0131 bulamad\\u0131k', 's